# design/handoff/ (frontend spec + prototype HTML) stays per-machine and
# NOT tracked (fermi-viewer convention); copy between machines manually or
# via OneDrive.
#
# plans/ was ignored under that same convention until 2026-08-09, when it
# was deliberately opted IN (owner decision): the plan tree is the thing
# multi-session work is carried out from, so it has to survive across
# machines and sessions with git history. Note this repo is public — treat
# plan contents as publicly visible and keep credentials, unpublished
# results and private-corpus paths out of them.
#
# plans/archive/ is ignored by DEFAULT (the 2026-08-09 opt-in covered the
# live plan tree only; legacy archived plans predate the public-visibility
# scrub), so a broad `git add` can never sweep an un-reviewed archived plan
# into a public commit. Archived plans that code comments cite by name are
# un-ignored individually below: a plan is the provenance record for the
# breadcrumbs in the modules it produced, so dropping it from the repo turns
# every one of those comments into a dangling pointer for anyone who clones.
# To un-ignore one, scrub it first (credentials, unpublished results,
# private-corpus paths) — this repo is public.
# NOTE the glob: `plans/archive/` would exclude the DIRECTORY, and git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so the negations below would be dead
# lines. `plans/archive/*` excludes the contents instead, leaving them
# reachable.
design/
plans/archive/*
!plans/archive/PROJECT_WORKFLOW_PLAN.md
!plans/archive/SPECTRAL_WORKSPACE_PLAN.md
!plans/archive/SHAPE_ANALYSIS_PLAN.md

